        },
        {
          "id": "bottom",
          "label": "bottom",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 90
        },
        {
          "id": "left",
          "label": "left",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "content-node"
        },
        "markdown": "## Read the graph as a separation of concerns\n\n**Content** owns durable material and its format. A **View** decides how that material is presented. A **Port** owns or delegates Views and supplies the graph interface.\n\nFollow the Question node next: scripting must author this structure without bypassing its invariants."
      }
    },
